## ThemeProvider

Wraps the application root and provides the active theme to all child components.

```tsx
import { ThemeProvider } from './design-system/theme/ThemeProvider';

<ThemeProvider brand="tesco" mode="light">
  <App />
</ThemeProvider>
```

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `brand` | `string` | `"tesco"` | Brand identifier (future multi-brand support) |
| `mode` | `"light" \| "dark"` | `"light"` | Colour mode (currently single theme) |
| `children` | `ReactNode` | — | Required |

## useTheme

Access the active theme from any component inside `ThemeProvider`.

```tsx
import { useTheme } from './design-system/theme/useTheme';

function MyComponent() {
  const { theme } = useTheme();

  return (
    <View style={{ backgroundColor: theme.background.colorBackground1 }}>
      ...
    </View>
  );
}
```

### Return value

```ts
{
  theme: {
    typography:       { colorTextHeaderPrimary, colorTextBody, ... }
    interaction:      { colorInteractiveDefault, colorInteractiveActive, ... }
    line:             { colorBorderPrimary, colorBorderSecondary }
    background:       { colorBackground1, colorBackground2 }
    typographyTokens: { family, weight, size12..size64, lineHeight16..lineHeight68 }
    spacing:          { none, xs, sm, md, lg, xl, xxl }
    borderRadius:     { sm, md, lg, pill }
  }
  brand: string
  mode: "light" | "dark"
}
```

## Goal

Migrate from bare React Native to **Expo SDK 53** by changing the minimum number of files, proving that the screen and design system are fully portable.

## The 5-file migration delta

```
git diff phase-1/bare-rn phase-2/expo -- src/
# Output: (empty) — zero screen/design-system changes
```

| File | Phase 1 | Phase 2 |
|------|---------|---------|
| `package.json` | `react-native start` scripts | `expo start` scripts, expo SDK added |
| `app.json` | `{ "name": "DDSNativeShell" }` | Full Expo config with platforms, bundleId |
| `babel.config.js` | `@react-native/babel-preset` | `babel-preset-expo` |
| `metro.config.js` | `@react-native/metro-config` | `expo/metro-config` |
| `index.js` | `AppRegistry.registerComponent(...)` | `registerRootComponent(App)` |

## Key changes explained

### `babel.config.js`

```js
// Phase 1
module.exports = { presets: ['module:@react-native/babel-preset'] };

// Phase 2
module.exports = (api) => {
  api.cache(true);
  return { presets: ['babel-preset-expo'] };
};
```

`babel-preset-expo` is a superset — it includes all bare RN transforms plus web support.

### `metro.config.js`

```js
// Phase 1
const { getDefaultConfig, mergeConfig } = require('@react-native/metro-config');

// Phase 2
const { getDefaultConfig } = require('expo/metro-config');
```

### `index.js`

```js
// Phase 1
import { AppRegistry } from 'react-native';
AppRegistry.registerComponent(appName, () => App);

// Phase 2
import { registerRootComponent } from 'expo';
registerRootComponent(App);
```

